	 <note id="GUID-9EE6BFC6-C61D-4231-94C8-D70CC05D2414"> Preliminary values and subject to change. 
		<p> 
		  <sup>1</sup> NVL and PTL DF, Ψ<sub>sn -hp</sub> are calculated using Intel Technology Targets based on most up to date test data. 
		</p> 
		<p> 
		  <sup>2</sup> DF<sub>Thermal_Solution</sub> is sensitive to the nature of the workload, Ψ<sub>sn-hp</sub> and Ψ<sub>hp-a</sub> are less sensitive to the nature of workload. 
		</p> 
		<p> 
		  <sup>3</sup> The transient performance for the first 5-10sis largely insensitive to Ψ<sub>hp-a</sub> and the heat exchanger should be sized for sustained power. Refer turbo workloads on page 29 for details on the RPM effect on the temperature increase and additional design guidance for improved transient performance. 
		</p> 
		<p><sup> 4</sup> The thermal solution used is 0.5mm cold plate soldered to 2 heat pipes (2 nos. of original diameter of 6mm crushed to 1.4mm). 
		</p> 
		<p> 
		  <sup>5</sup> The thermal solution used is 1.3mm cold plate soldered to 2 heat pipes (2 nos. of original diameter of 6mm crushed to 1.4mm, 1 no. of original diameter of 8mm crushed to 1.6mm). 
		</p> 
		<p><sup> 6</sup>The thermal solution used is 3mm cold plate soldered to 2 heat pipes (1 no. of original diameter of 8mm crushed to 2mm, 1 no. of original diameter of 10mm crushed to 2mm). 
		</p> 
	 </note> 
